      "full": "H5154. nechushah נְחוּשָׁה and ( Lev 26:19 ; Job 40:18 ) נְחֻשָׁה noun feminine copper, bronze (only in poetry; compare I. נְחשֶׁת ); — ׳נ always absolute; — 1 copper produced from ore by melting Job 28:2 . 2 copper , doubtless hardened with alloy, = bronze , as material of bow 2Sam 22:35 = Psa 18:35 ; Job 20:24 ; gates Isa 45:2 ; figurative of strength Job 40:18 (bones of hippopotamus), compare 41:19 , Micah 4:13 (hoofs of Zion); of obstinate brow Isa 48:4 (|| עָרְמֶּ֑ךָ בַּרְזֶל גִּיד ); unproductive earth Lev 26:19 .",
